  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0056 database is used for storing information about abilities, assigned roles, permissions, and roles. The abilities table contains information about the abilities that can be assigned to roles, including the ability name, title, entity ID, entity type, whether the ability is only owned, options, scope, created at, and updated at timestamps. The assigned_roles table contains information about the roles that have been assigned to entities, including the role ID, entity ID, entity type, restricted to ID, restricted to type, scope, and created at and updated at timestamps. The permissions table contains information about the permissions that have been assigned to abilities, including the ability ID, entity ID, entity type, whether the permission is forbidden, scope, and created at and updated at timestamps. The roles table contains information about the roles, including the role name, title, level, scope, created at, and updated at timestamps. The abilities, assigned_roles, permissions, and roles tables are connected through foreign keys, with the abilities table referencing the roles table, the assigned_roles table referencing the roles and abilities tables, and the permissions table referencing the abilities table.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context:\nThe project focuses on creating a permissions and roles management system for applications built on the Laravel framework. The system leverages Eloquent models to define and manage roles and abilities through an authorization package named Bouncer. Bouncer is developed by Joseph Silber and operates with a framework-agnostic approach, allowing seamless integration with Laravel's authorization gates.\n\n2) Objectives:\nThe main objective is to provide a flexible, expressive way to manage user roles and permissions within Laravel applications. The system aims to stay unobtrusive, allowing developers to integrate custom code alongside Bouncer's capabilities.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:\n- Developers: Implementing the role and permissions management system in Laravel applications.\n- Application Users: Individuals whose roles and abilities are defined using the system.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:\n- Role Management: Define roles with associated abilities.\n- Ability Management: Create and manage abilities that can be attached to roles or users.\n- Authorization Gate: Use Bouncer to define authorization checks for different actions.\n- Integration Flexibility: Allows integration with existing app capabilities and precedence to custom code.\n- Database Integration: Utilizes Eloquent models to manage data related to roles, abilities, and permissions.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:\n- Framework Agnostic: Designed to work primarily with Laravel but maintains flexibility for other frameworks.\n- Expressive Syntax: Facilitates an easy-to-understand configuration pathway for developers.\n- Performance: Efficiently handle authorization without significant impact on application performance.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0056.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0056\nCREATE TABLE `abilities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `ability_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `is_only_owned` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `options` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `scope` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `abilities_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`entity_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `assigned_roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `restricted_to_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `restricted_to_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `scope` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `assigned_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `assigned_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`entity_id`) REFERENCES `abilities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `ability_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entity_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `is_forbidden` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `scope` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ability_id`) REFERENCES `abilities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scope` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
